  "tail": "Completed Batch 10’s draft items and A/B pages. The A page contains the stratified design, unbiasedness and variance result, and fixed size and fixed cost allocation theorems. The B page has worked examples for proportional allocation, zero variance, and rounding.\n\nSource coverage records three treatments: [Shalabh, Chapter 4](https://home.iitk.ac.in/~shalab/sampling/chapter4-sampling-stratified-sampling.pdf), [STAT392, Chapter 8](https://homepages.ecs.vuw.ac.nz/~rarnold/STAT392/SampleSurveysBook/_book/stratified-sampling), and [Wright’s Census Bureau report](https://www.census.gov/content/dam/Census/library/working-papers/2014/adrm/rrs2014-07.pdf). All three passed `source-fetch-check`.\n\nThe seven Step 1 records are **escalated**: the actual supplier bodies were checked, but `def-finite-population-and-sampling-design` and `thm-horvitz-thompson-total-is-design-unbiased` still have unresolved upstream readiness records. The active run remains owner-held; I did not change its state.\n\nScoped precheck, proof layout, rendering, dependency checks, content policy, and proof-contract validation passed. The batch 10 item levels recomputed as 4, 6, 7, 7, 7, 8, 8. Full-run dependency checks also encountered unrelated manifest and YAML parse blockers; details and exact evidence are in the [batch notes](</home/lazyinspirit/Projects/prestige-math-library/research/statistical-models-experiments-62-batch-10.notes.md>).\n\nFiles: [A page](/home/lazyinspirit/Projects/prestige-math-library/library/statistical-models-and-experiments/stratified-sampling-and-allocation.md), [B page](/home/lazyinspirit/Projects/prestige-math-library/library/statistical-models-and-experiments/stratified-sampling-and-allocation-examples.md), [manifest](/home/lazyinspirit/Projects/prestige-math-library/research/statistical-models-experiments-62-batch-10.pages.json), [proof contracts](/home/lazyinspirit/Projects/prestige-math-library/research/statistical-models-experiments-62-batch-10.proof-contracts.json), [source coverage](/home/lazyinspirit/Projects/prestige-math-library/research/statistical-models-experiments-62-batch-10.coverage.json), and [cross-batch dependencies](/home/lazyinspirit/Projects/prestige-math-library/research/statistical-models-experiments-62-batch-10.cross-batch-dependencies.json)."
